WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.689
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie. Hopefully you
guys have had a chance to see the first episode.

00:00:05.689 --> 00:00:10.320
Since this is our first time seeing Peter
Capaldi as The Doctor in a proper story most

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:17.320
of this video is going to be spent on him.
But there’s a lot of talk about what’s

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:22.630
happening with Clara and TV Guide even spoiled
a few big things. So once I get through the

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.750
important stuff I’ll address all that.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.980
If you’re just finding me for the first
time I’m doing weekly doctor who videos

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.070
for all the episodes. And a weekly giveaway.
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.480
and leave a comment. I’ll announce the winner
when I post my Q&amp;A video tomorrow.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.930
So important stuff first, Top 10 moments from
the premiere. Careful for spoilers if you

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:41.190
haven’t seen it yet. I’ll wait just a
sec...okay. Here we got. Number 10 - The New

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.320
Title Sequence

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.750
I feel like this is going to be one of the
more controversial changes to the show. I

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.450
knew they’d change them to suit the tone
of Capaldi’s run but I didn’t think they’d

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.270
change this much.

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.870
There’s actually a cool story as to why
they went with the pocket watch over the time

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:59.579
vortex. There was a fan who made his own clockwork
titles, steven moffat saw them and thought

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:01.120
it would be a good update.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.180
The final version they use on the show is
different from what the fan originally made.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.310
His name is Billy Hanshaw. He’s a professional
graphics designer so he makes titles like

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:14.920
these for a living but it’s still really
cool to think Steven Moffat made a change

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.689
this big based on something a fan did.

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:24.299
Moffat said it was the best idea for a change
to the titles he’d seen since 1963. Depending

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:29.909
on what you count as a title edit there have
been over 13 versions, here’s a quick montage

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:36.909
of them all.

00:01:39.429 --> 00:01:41.159
Number 9 - The Grand Entrance

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:45.509
I always like that no matter what the Doctor’s
personality is, he always makes a grand stage

00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:49.770
entrance and getting spit up by a dinosaur
is a nice addition to the deck of cards that

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.869
comprise all the doctor’s first introductions.

00:01:52.869 --> 00:01:58.429
Most of the interviews Capaldi has been doing
peg his Doctor as uncaring but I think the

00:01:58.429 --> 00:02:00.779
bit with slamming the door in Strax’s face
does a really good job of showing how funny

00:02:00.779 --> 00:02:06.969
it’s going to be despite the new pro-Robot
Suicide Doctor.

00:02:06.969 --> 00:02:12.939
Matt Smith was quick with the jokes but I
feel like Capaldi nails the dry wit of british

00:02:12.939 --> 00:02:16.189
humor perfectly. If any of you guys from the
UK want to explain the difference between

00:02:16.189 --> 00:02:20.280
british humor and American humor please do,
personally I think it’s all about the subtle

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.629
turn of phrase. Being clever and biting in
a very casual way.

00:02:24.629 --> 00:02:29.360
Capaldi insults everyone that walks into his
field of vision, but turns out it’s okay.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:30.379
Because he’s gone Scottish.

00:02:30.379 --> 00:02:34.780
That by the way was my favorite quote from
the episode. “Have I gone Scottish?” “Now

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.739
I can REALLY complain about things!”

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:42.319
Just for reference, David Tennant, Karen Gillan
and Steven Moffat are all Scottish in real

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:46.480
life too. But David Tennant didn’t lean
on his Scottish accent when he took the role

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.030
of the tenth doctor. Peter Capaldi made special
mention that he would be keeping his Scottish

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:54.010
accent during his run. And I think it’s
great.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:56.209
Number 8 - Clara Reacts To Peter Capaldi

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:59.999
What would you do if the person you loved
changed their face. I guess you could consider

00:02:59.999 --> 00:03:04.439
that a joke about plastic surgery. But really
this is Clara’s first experience with a

00:03:04.439 --> 00:03:09.280
regeneration. Vastra and Jenny were a nice
analogy for what the ideal version of a relationship

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.269
should be.

00:03:10.269 --> 00:03:15.489
Loving someone no matter how they change.
This whole episode was meta in that it’s

00:03:15.489 --> 00:03:19.420
Clara getting used to the new doctor and we
as the fandom getting used to him. So for

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.999
a lot of the episode we’re viewing things
from Clara’s perspective.

00:03:22.999 --> 00:03:26.780
When Vastra put him to sleep and Clara heard
him whispering he had this really poetic speech

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:32.269
about how alone he really is. He even said
it later to the Robot Leader, I don’t expect

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:35.810
to make it to paradise. Which is just a metaphor
for Gallifrey.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:39.469
He is utterly alone. Which is why the companion
relationship is going to be so important this

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:43.780
series. Capaldi’s Doctor is more afraid
that ever, which might explain why he insults

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:46.379
people so much. Usually that’s a red flag
for insecurity.

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:51.340
I tried to find a reference to the speech
he whispered, “All the world is grey and

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:52.120
I am alone.”

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:58.620
All I could think of was Metaltron from Series
1. Metaltron and the 9th Doctor have that

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:05.620
conversation where the Dalek ponders it’s
loneliness. The Doctor also said the Dinosaur

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.599
was all alone too.

00:04:10.599 --> 00:04:15.299
The Doctor is utterly lonely but for some
reason he doesn’t like hugs. I love how

00:04:15.299 --> 00:04:21.259
funny some of the contradictions in his personality
are. The hugging part seems like a very Victorian

00:04:21.259 --> 00:04:25.139
british thing too. Not being outwardly affectionate,
especially in public.

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:29.090
Which leads me to Number 7 - The doctor isn’t
cuddly anymore

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:33.949
This is taken from a Neil Gaiman Quote after
he first saw the episode. One of the major

00:04:33.949 --> 00:04:38.440
differences in Capaldi’s portrayal is a
Doctor that doesn’t yearn for affection.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.889
Not flirting, don’t get any ideas.

00:04:40.889 --> 00:04:45.680
When he said that line all I could think of
was River and all the attractive female companions

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.620
from Classic Who till now. Not all Doctors
before Capaldi were flirty, it’s mostly

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:56.620
something that the show has pushed forward
since the 2005 series began.

00:04:56.919 --> 00:05:02.050
The cuddly part is all Matt Smith. I never
found it off putting but I was still pretty

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:06.220
new to the series when he started in 2011.
I didn’t see a lot of the Darker Doctor’s

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:07.150
till later.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:11.710
I think about half of you guys loved Smith
and the other half thought a cuddly Doctor

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:12.419
was rubbish.

00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:18.110
I’m really interested to see how much darker
Capaldi gets. There were a couple scenes that

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:21.610
summed him up pretty well that i’ll explain
in a sec.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.840
on to Number 6 - The Doctor and Clara get
to know each other again

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.360
Loved the banter, they seem more like an old
married couple or a couple of really old friends.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:33.240
Making fun of each other without taking it
too seriously. The doctor makes fun of her

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:34.830
vanity, clara makes fun of his grey hair.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.960
Both of them are saying this is who I am,
I’m not going to change. But it doesn’t

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:38.800
mean we’re not friends.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.639
I got such a Sherlock vibe from the whole
episode but the restaurant pre-capture was

00:05:44.639 --> 00:05:48.810
a good example of a conversation Sherlock
would have with Watson. Their relationship

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.949
is a good metaphor for Clara and the Doctor’s
relationship.

00:05:51.949 --> 00:05:56.520
The Doctor is the brilliant but crazy one
and Clara is the sensible one who serves as

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:01.120
his interpreter when he starts speaking gibberish
or gets too rude.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.770
There were also a lot of obvious sherlock
references too. Like Vastra saying “The

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:07.509
Game is Afoot”, “There’s a murder, the
Doctor has taken the case”.

00:06:07.509 --> 00:06:11.479
Steven Moffat said that he was totally open
to the idea of a Wholock story if Benedict

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:18.479
Cumberbatch and Peter Capaldi’s schedules
ever worked out.

00:06:19.259 --> 00:06:21.849
Number 5 - The Rubbish Robots from the Dawn
of Time

00:06:21.849 --> 00:06:25.659
The were reports from a long time ago that
the Clockwork Droids from Girl in the Fireplace

00:06:25.659 --> 00:06:31.259
would be back. The doctor kept referencing
the episode by saying this all sounds familiar.

00:06:31.259 --> 00:06:37.159
And even held up that logo.
Just to be clear. The ship in Deep Breath

00:06:37.159 --> 00:06:42.889
was the Marie Antoinette and it was the Sister
Ship of the Madame de Pompadour. The Pompadour

00:06:42.889 --> 00:06:46.960
was the ship from Girl in the fireplace, so
these droids were not the same ones.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.199
They were based on the same technology, but
it’s a different group of robots. Searching

00:06:51.199 --> 00:06:52.090
for paradise.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:55.699
I’ll talk more about Paradise in a sec,
because that ties in with the villain and

00:06:55.699 --> 00:06:56.479
the finale this year.

00:06:56.479 --> 00:07:00.000
But Number 4- There Doctor Doesn’t Ever
Expect To Get Home

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.259
This was another Rule number 1 moment where
I couldn’t tell if the Doctor was lying.

00:07:05.259 --> 00:07:10.419
If you believe Matt Smith is in there, then
he’s taking the long way round back to Gallifrey.

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:13.259
So he does expect to get home.

00:07:13.259 --> 00:07:16.699
I think he was just saying whatever it took
to get the leader to jump out of the skin

00:07:16.699 --> 00:07:18.360
balloon ship. I

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:24.449
I loved how he confronted the robot throwing
his immortality in his face. “There is no

00:07:24.449 --> 00:07:29.150
trace of you left.” Capaldi can’t remember
where he got his face from, like he’s talking

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:30.930
to himself as much as he’s talking to the
robot.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:35.669
He also had that line earlier in the episode
when he got his first set of clothes. He looked

00:07:35.669 --> 00:07:39.520
in the mirror and said “I’ve seen this
face before” “But I didn’t make the

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.280
frown lines”.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:44.949
I’ve seen theories that this is a reference
to Capaldi’s character from Fires of Pompeii.

00:07:44.949 --> 00:07:48.969
Meaning that the doctor could have chosen
that face as a sign that he really does care

00:07:48.969 --> 00:07:52.409
despite it being against his nature as a time
lord.

00:07:52.409 --> 00:07:59.159
In fires of pompeii he went back to save the
capaldi character, which was against his rules.

00:07:59.159 --> 00:08:04.719
He cared so much he broke his own rules. So
it’s possible that the explanation of his

00:08:04.719 --> 00:08:08.419
face is that he chose it to remind himself
that he cares. Even though he’s supposed

00:08:08.419 --> 00:08:12.139
to be the not-caring doctor.

00:08:12.139 --> 00:08:16.300
Then he turns on a dime and pretty much says
he does have it in him to murder in order

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:23.300
to protect his friends. Which is super dark.
We can talk about this one scene all day.

00:08:24.449 --> 00:08:29.530
This is what Capaldi’s doctor is all about.
Fierce and distant but not uncaring.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:33.240
and Number 3 - The New TARDIS

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:39.210
Everybody pointed out the bookshelves in the
trailer, but here we can see him sitting in

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:44.960
a chair just like the seventh Doctor. His
TARDIS was made to look more victorian so

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:48.780
when Peter Capaldi’s debut was announced
as a victorian episode I wondered if there

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:51.850
was a connection
Really there are very minor changes structurally.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:58.850
It’s just a color pallette shift. It’s
dark lighting with warm colors. Which I think

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:04.690
is just a callback to his personality. Outwardly
very dark but still bigger and warmer on the

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:05.410
inside.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:09.720
Lots of great references to old doctor’s
tardises here though. Especially the round

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:14.380
things. That was one of the funniest references
from the 50th Anniversary when Smith and Tennant

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.980
saw John Hurt’s Tardis.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:17.800
They were also confused by the round things.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.740
Just to explain that, for several seasons
the first couple of doctor’s tardises all

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:26.450
had round things. Even the 9th doctor’s
tardis in 2005 had the round rivets.

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:29.120
But Number 2 - Phone Call from Trenzalore

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:33.060
This was spoiled pretty early on, but I still
enjoyed it all the same. Matt Smith came back

00:09:33.060 --> 00:09:36.750
to do the scene, they didn’t film that during
the Christmas Special.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:42.300
It’s just a way for Peter Capaldi’s Doctor
to explain time lord regeneration to Clara.

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.980
They’re all the same person even though
the faces and personalities change. Thus the

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:46.450
no hugging.

00:09:46.450 --> 00:09:51.340
I did like that Matt Smith made jokes about
Capaldi being old. Doctor Who does the best

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:54.140
job of making fun of itself without going
too far.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:57.630
But my Number 1 moment was The Woman, Missy.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:01.290
I am convinced this is not River Song despite
all the boyfriend talk. I know a lot of you

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:03.660
have Rani theories. But let me point out something
really interesting. Moffat Referred to her

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.700
as the Gatekeeper of the Nethersphere and
she appears in the two part finale. So she

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:08.490
is very important.

00:10:08.490 --> 00:10:13.530
But her paradise callout is also really interesting
because we have no idea what the nethersphere

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:19.710
is and this garden looks mysteriously like
the garden Amy Pond got stuck in during The

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:21.550
Girl Who Waited.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:26.660
In that episode, paradise was literally a
resort planet called Apalapucia. So it’s

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:29.980
possible that the clockwork droid was transported
there by Missy.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:35.460
There’s also the thematic link to the girl
who waited episode too. In it, the doctor

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:40.130
choses to leave Amy Behind to die. So does
that mean that capaldi is going to have to

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.040
make the same choice.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.210
I don’t think it’s a coincidence that
he did it when they were on the clockwork

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:48.780
ship. Even though he came back. It might just
be foreshadowing that he’ll have to leave

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:51.340
clara behind for real at some point this season.
Just something to think about.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:56.130
And then there’s the bit about the woman
that gave clara the doctor’s number. Capaldi

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:00.320
even says that whoever she is, she’s very
keen on keeping Clara and the Doctor together.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:05.270
That woman of course is Missy. So why does
missy want clara to remain with the doctor?

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:10.880
I’ll save some of my missy theories until
after we learn some more about her. I don’t

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.720
want to jump to Rani too soon. But clearly
she has known multiple versions of the Doctor,

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:20.550
and there are very few females in the universe
that are as long lived as the timelords.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:24.150
Let me know what your favorite things from
the episode were and what you think of capaldi

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:25.030
so far.

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:28.250
Here’s a couple quick easter eggs before
my review.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:32.550
The person early in the episode who gets his
eyes stolen is Ser Dontos from Game of Thrones.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:35.700
Which is funny given how each of those characters
ended up.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:40.620
The Sonic Devices that Strax, Vastra and Jenny
used in the episode were designed by fans

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.330
in a Blue Peter contest last year.

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:46.130
And possibly my favorite easter egg was the
scarf. When Capaldi’s going on about clothes

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:49.510
he says he needs a long scar, but the backtracks
quickly say, no that’d look stupid.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.920
I imagine Tom Baker laughed pretty hard when
he saw that.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:56.430
It also sounds like the Doctor gave his pocketwatch
to the man to get those clothes, which I think

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:59.300
could come back to bite him in the ass.

00:11:59.300 --> 00:12:06.300
There were a lot more so if you saw references
to other episodes write them in the comments.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:15.150
Overall I gave the episode a solid A for being
so different and hypnotizing despite using

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:17.630
a lot of old things from Moffat’s run like
the clockwork droids. Peter Capaldi said it

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:21.090
best in the episode, I’ve seen this before.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:27.030
I felt like the use of the paternoster foreshadows
a potential spinoff. I don’t expect it to

00:12:27.030 --> 00:12:30.950
happen, but I felt like this episode asked
more from those characters in terms of performance

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:35.700
than any previous episode they’ve appeared
in. As if to show that they can carry a show

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.450
without The Doctor.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:42.180
I am so enjoying this new Grumpy Scottish
Doctor and based on what Moffat has said about

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:49.180
each of the episodes this series I think it’s
going to be a lot of fun. I did a video summing

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.580
up all of what he said, I’ll add a link
to it at the end.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:57.210
In related news, my Q&amp;A for this will post
Sunday, so hopefully everyone will have a

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.860
chance to rewatch the episode and come up
with questions.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.630
I’ll also announce the winner of the giveaway
when I post that. Remember all you have to

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:08.880
do to enter is be a subscriber and leave a
comment on this video. It’s open to international

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:09.460
people too.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:12.930
You can get the Q&amp;A video by clicking here.
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:18.230
it. And click here for the full Series 8 Schedule
with Moffat’s explanations for everything.

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:23.860
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.
Now let’s all high five and rewatch the

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:24.490
episode.

